{"id":"abishag","name":"Abishag","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:abishag"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Abishag","text":"Father of (i.e., “given to”) error, a young woman of Shunem, distinguished for her beauty. She was chosen to minister to David in his old age. She became his wife (1 Kings 1:3, 4, 15). After David’s death Adonijah persuaded Bathsheba, Solomon’s mother, to entreat the king to permit him to marry Abishag. Solomon suspected in this request an aspiration to the throne, and therefore caused him to be put to death (1 Kings 2:17-25)."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H138","lemma":"אֲדֹנִיָּה","xlit":"ʼĂdônîyâh","gloss":"Adonijah, the name of three Israelites","kjv":"Adonijah","count":6,"share":0.35},{"strong":"H49","lemma":"אֲבִישַׁג","xlit":"ʼĂbîyshag","gloss":"Abishag, a concubine of David","kjv":"Abishag","count":4,"share":0.24},{"strong":"H7767","lemma":"שׁוּנַמִּית","xlit":"Shûwnammîyth","gloss":"a Shunammitess, or female inhabitant of Shunem","kjv":"Shunamite","count":4,"share":0.24},{"strong":"H8010","lemma":"שְׁלֹמֹה","xlit":"Shᵉlômôh","gloss":"Shelomah, David's successor","kjv":"Solomon","count":6,"share":0.35},{"strong":"H1339","lemma":"בַּת־שֶׁבַע","xlit":"Bath-Shebaʻ","gloss":"Bath-Sheba, the mother of Solomon","kjv":"Bath-sheba","count":3,"share":0.18},{"strong":"H517","lemma":"אֵם","xlit":"ʼêm","gloss":"a mother","kjv":"dam, mother, parting","count":4,"share":0.24}],"verses":["1Kgs.2.13","1Kgs.2.19","1Kgs.2.21","1Kgs.2.22","1Kgs.2.23","1Kgs.2.24","1Kgs.1.1","1Kgs.1.2","1Kgs.1.3","1Kgs.1.4","1Kgs.2.14","1Kgs.2.15","1Kgs.2.16","1Kgs.2.17","1Kgs.2.18","1Kgs.2.20","1Kgs.2.25"],"related":[{"id":"adonijah","type":"cooccur","shared":13,"jaccard":0.565,"why":"13 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"shunammite","type":"cooccur","shared":14,"jaccard":0.298,"why":"14 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"bath-sheba-bathsheba","type":"cooccur","shared":9,"jaccard":0.209,"why":"9 verses are indexed under both"},{